     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EIF Tier 2 Project Team has been working with small holder producers &amp; businesses to:
- improve their participation in selected value chains &amp; increase their connectivity to markets. This means seeking out intra-island , regional &amp; international trade opportunities, including linking to buyers through networks such as PTI NZ and PTI Australia; 
- offer training to improve production practices at various levels of the value chainand supporting MSMEs to comply with export standards. 
- Ensuring equity, the EIF Project Team has made it a focus on Tier 2 to incorporate gender and environmental awareness trainings.
- To date Over 300 participants (including 145 women and 100 youth) have participated in EIF trainings to improve their participation in value chains. 
This training has contributed to value addition in key sectors namely Agriculture and Fisheries thus paving the way for market penetration in new markets in 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
